KNOWN-DEFECTIVE SNAPSHOT — do not demo or cherry-pick from this commit.

Package A5 (Connections) is in-progress here and an adversarial review found
seven defects in exactly this code, three of them HIGH:

  1. The board partition is fully recoverable from the served response. The
     shuffle seed is sha256(nonce), the nonce is plaintext inside the board
     token, and the pre-shuffle rows are ordered grouped 4/4/4/4 — so a client
     can replay the PRNG and read off every tile's group. Verified: exact
     partition recovered on every trial.
  2. points.maxMistakes is never enforced server-side, so busting the mistake
     budget scores strictly better than stopping honestly.
  3. Connections points never reach the lifetime score, and accrual is written
     on two different event rows, so widening the stats filter double-counts.

Plus: floorPenalty charged on abandoned boards; lever:'none' leaking through
sessionStorage into the quiz's research log; board_reported_ambiguous carrying
no board id; a dead-end on a duplicate board-complete.

Nothing here was student-reachable — the registry row is enabled:false — and
no board content was ever loaded. Fixes land in a follow-up commit.
